	quest.70A627EADC8BFAC6.quest_desc: [
		"After you've taken the photos you want with the color film, begin developing it by combining it with a &bMundane Potion&r, &bAwkward Potion&r, and &bThick Potion&r to get the developed film roll."
		""
		"Once you have the developed roll, move on to the light room!"
	]
	quest.70A627EADC8BFAC6.quest_subtitle: "Click to learn more!"
	quest.715A095CC8D42FEB.quest_desc: [
		"Feed 256,000 items or buckets of fluid into the Matter Condenser while in Singularity mode."
		"I recommend a &6Create&r cobble generator or hose pully on the ocean with a lot of pumps."
	]
	quest.717A0F8A80A048AC.quest_desc: [
		"The Wireless Terminal is essentially the baby brother of the Advanced Wireless Terminal."
		""
		"Despite its name implying \"wireless\" functionality, it's not truly wireless. This tier of the wireless terminal simply enables you to access the storage terminal or crafting terminal from approximately 17 blocks away. However, it requires line of sight to the terminals, and you must right-click while holding it to open the grid."
		""
		"It's highly recommended to upgrade to the advanced tier as soon as possible for enhanced functionality."
	]
	quest.717A0F8A80A048AC.quest_subtitle: "Click to learn more!"
	quest.7183BB6CFEBF4651.quest_subtitle: "Used to teach Pokémon moves. (Infinite Use)"
	quest.718BABEFE51DBC00.title: "Obtain 1024x Warped Stem"
	quest.71F9A1A2059F9144.quest_desc: ["Good for things like Metal Ingots and Coins"]
	quest.71F9A1A2059F9144.quest_subtitle: "Combines/Separates twice"
	quest.7261B1D905784667.quest_desc: [
		"Need to include a Storage Drawer Controller or other non-AE inventories? This is how."
		""
		"Be careful, as connecting large &l&4cluttered containers full of NBT items will cause server performance issues&r&r. It is identical to the infamous Tom's Simple Storage problem that got Tom's replaced with AE2 in Mayview in the first place. Tom's uses these for all its storage."
		""
		"It's also why Cells have Type restrictions. You can at most cram 630 nonstackables into an ME Drive before you run out of room, compared to millions of normal items. You can literally corrupt world saves or chunkban/bookban yourself with this if you're reckless enough, though the more common case is just building a lag-machine by accident."
		""
		"Examples of things that have a lot of NBT data are most non-stackable items, like written books, enchanted tools, banners, and very long custom names. Storage Cells and Components that still contain items especially have a LOT of NBT data. I wouldn't recommend throwing in a full Storage Drawer either, just to be safe."
	]
	quest.7261B1D905784667.quest_subtitle: "For inventorying non-AE inventories"
	quest.72C9825C4040E66C.quest_desc: ["The Inventory Cable Connector works similarly to the Inventory Connector block, but it will only read the inventory it is directly connected to and no other inventory. This can be useful for reading the output of single storage blocks like Drawers or Barrels that aren't near your bulk storage area. Additionally, it can be used as a platform to place a terminal on."]
	quest.72C9825C4040E66C.quest_subtitle: "Click to learn more!"
	quest.732E63D8FE0AF497.quest_subtitle: "Slow and fuel-hungry, but carries an entire storage."
	quest.73614F77165F238C.quest_subtitle: "Obtained by killing hoglins with a knife,"
	quest.73C4BF145A20C5E7.quest_desc: ["A &bFroglight&r drops from a &4Magma Cube&r when it's killed by a &bFrog&r. The type of &bFroglight&r that drops depends on the type of &bFrog&r."]
	quest.73C4BF145A20C5E7.quest_subtitle: "Wait, you have to do WHAT?"
